// == TRACK 4 - LAYER 2 - MOTION ==============================================
// LIGHTCYCLE's hook: the light trail. Fast, bright, and mostly ASCENDING, which
// is the opposite of track 3's wave-shaped cell — a line that keeps climbing
// reads as accelerating, and this track wants the player leaning forward.
//
// The cell is root - 5th - octave - 5th, a broken power chord rather than a
// triad. No thirds anywhere in this layer: leaving the third out is what lets
// the Bb bars sit against the A pedal without the harmony resolving itself. The
// mode stays ambiguous and slightly wrong, which at speed reads as electric.
//
// The multiplier lives INSIDE each cell, never outside the slowcat. Outside, `*n`
// means n ITEMS PER CYCLE and the whole progression races past n times while the
// bass makes one pass — a bug that shipped in two other tracks here and was only
// caught by reading the events sidecar.
//
// Delay is a dotted 8th (0.375s at cps 0.5) so echoes land between the 16ths.
setcps(0.5)
stack(
  // THE TRAIL. Measured 3.5 dB quieter than the equivalent layer on the other
  // three tracks, which is most of why tier 2 used to arrive and change nothing.
  note(`<[[a4 e5 a5 e5]*4]
         [[a4 e5 a5 e5]*4]
         [[bb4 f5 bb5 f5]*4]
         [[bb4 f5 bb5 f5]*4]
         [[a4 e5 a5 e5]*4]
         [[a4 e5 a5 e5]*4]
         [[g4 d5 g5 d5]*4]
         [[f4 c5 f5 c5]*4]>`)
    .s("square")
    .lpf(sine.range(1400, 5200).slow(4)).lpq(7)   // twice as fast as track 3's
    .gain(0.23).release(0.04)
    .delay(0.32).delaytime(0.375).delayfeedback(0.34)
    .pan(0.54).room(0.16).size(0.6),

  // THE STAB — the instrument this track did not have, in the band it did not
  // cover. Everything else lives below 1.3 kHz (bass, filtered to 380-1250) or
  // above 1.4 kHz (trail, lead); nothing occupied 200 Hz - 1 kHz, which is
  // exactly where filtered house chords live. A hole that wide reads as thin
  // rather than as clean.
  //
  // It also fixes a rhythm problem. Bass, trail and hats were all on the 16th
  // grid at once, so nothing owned a subdivision and the layers blurred into
  // one texture instead of stacking. The stab is on OFFBEAT EIGHTHS — the only
  // voice in the track on that pulse — so it separates by rhythm as well as by
  // frequency. Kick on quarters, stab on offbeat eighths, trail on sixteenths,
  // bass on sixteenths-with-holes: four distinguishable pulses.
  //
  // Root-fifth-octave, still no third: the layer-3 lead is what states the mode,
  // and a stab this prominent stating it early would spend the payload.
  //
  // This replaces the triangle "shadow" trail that used to sit here. That voice
  // was offset by exactly one sixteenth — a whole grid step — so instead of two
  // lights running slightly out of step it simply doubled the trail and thickened
  // the same 16th grid. The dotted-eighth delay already on the trail does the
  // out-of-step job properly, because 0.375s is not a grid multiple.
  note(`<[[~ [a3,e4,a4]]*4]
         [[~ [a3,e4,a4]]*4]
         [[~ [bb3,f4,bb4]]*4]
         [[~ [bb3,f4,bb4]]*4]
         [[~ [a3,e4,a4]]*4]
         [[~ [a3,e4,a4]]*4]
         [[~ [g3,d4,g4]]*4]
         [[~ [f3,c4,f4]]*4]>`)
    .s("sawtooth")
    .lpf(sine.range(520, 1150).slow(8)).lpq(11)
    .attack(0.002).decay(0.13).sustain(0)
    .gain(0.20).pan(0.44).room(0.2).size(0.55)
)
